        "raisedBy": [
          "performance"
        ],
        "recommendation": "The loop of `monthly_report` (`src/report.rs:23-30`) calls, through `customer_label` (`src/report.rs:26`), `db.customer` (`SELECT ... FROM customers WHERE id = $1`) once per invoice, so a report runs 1 + N + 1 queries: about 3 000 round trips for a month of 3 000 invoices from only 800 customers, and the count grows with the month's invoices. `Db::customers(&[i64])` (`WHERE id = ANY($1)`) already serves the whole set in one query: collect the distinct `customer_id`s, fetch them once, index them in a `HashMap<i64, Customer>` and build each label from it. Keep the current behavior when a customer is missing (an error), and keep the invoice-number order.",
